{"title":"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems\">2005 AMC 12B #11</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10B Problems\">2005 AMC 10B #15</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Quick_if_no_time)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Quick if no time)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Quick_and_simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Quick and simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An envelope contains eight bills: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ones, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> fives, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tens, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> twenties.  Two bills are drawn at random without replacement.  What is the probability that their sum is &#36;<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or more?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/1925481673aac1e5b54fe39080c98d64f4f868e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\ {{{\\frac{1}{4}}}} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\ {{{\\frac{2}{5}}}} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\ {{{\\frac{3}{7}}}} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\ {{{\\frac{1}{2}}}} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\ {{{\\frac{2}{3}}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"403\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The only way to get a total of \\$<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or more is if you pick a twenty and another bill, or if you pick both tens. There are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a819257864b33269141d19f1d7f14adecdc88ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{8}{2}=\\dfrac{8\\times7}{2\\times1}=28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"147\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bills out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose a twenty and some other non-twenty bill. There is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way to choose both twenties, and also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way to choose both tens. Adding these up, we find that there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ways to attain a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or greater, so there is a total probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9afac7412a7a7f338c7dee18a29ec83ed9604fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{14}{28}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"108\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another way to do this problem is to use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_counting\" title=\"Complementary counting\">complementary counting</a>, i.e. how many ways that the sum is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Now, you do not have to consider the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> twenties, so you have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bills left. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a138d1cd3d5560e0c9e7bec9576f68ea73d54cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{6}{2} = \\dfrac{6\\times5}{2\\times1} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"150\" height=\"55\" /> ways. However, you counted the case when you have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tens, so you need to subtract 1, and you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Finding the ways to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or higher, you subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/3/a63a0e529e87987f9803008af272714e110746fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{14}{28} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }\\dfrac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"108\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two cases that work, namely getting at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> twenty, or getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tens.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1be0245389ea2fdad5a0eb26a17b9f812e0bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\text{Get at least one twenty}) = 1-P(\\text{Do not get a single twenty})=1- \\frac{\\binom{6}{2}}{\\binom{8}{2}}=\\frac{28-15}{28}=\\frac{13}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"689\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b10462ec3bf763a1f65a850b22aeea89b8c127.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\text{Get two tens}) = \\frac{1}{\\binom{8}{2}} = \\frac{1}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"217\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Summing up our cases, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf76b2bb92f792d964698fb471fb227a6a982c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13}{28}+\\frac{1}{28}=\\frac{14}{28}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\dfrac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"199\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that if a twenty is drawn, anything else that is drawn will create a total greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />; The probability of a twenty being drawn first is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cf72c5136384cd1309126dbfb90b4237a20df2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"16\" height=\"37\" /> The same could be said for drawing anything, and then drawing a twenty. However, we can only draw something that isn't a twenty first (since we've already accounted for the probability of drawing two twenties). \n</p><p>The probability of drawing a non-twenty first, then a twenty second is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1c0b19a7ad365afa4a92567c6e1abff611c9de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot\\frac{2}{7}=\\frac{3}{14}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> Finally, we can draw two tens. The probability of this occuring is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/d/31d0e070f0b18293608d360f86e89c150722b313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot\\frac{1}{7}=\\frac{1}{28}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>Adding these three probabilities gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed004f5b587c5d63907619e3ecb4ba79ccc9770a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{14}+\\frac{1}{28}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\dfrac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"188\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath1) (edited by AMC_8)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Quick_if_no_time.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Quick_if_no_time)\">Solution 5 (Quick if no time)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Quick if no time)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of each bill. We can simplify the question to only drawing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> bill out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and trying to draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07acdb21ef213686516af033784fad961497677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />. (Originally you need to draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a952bdac436c12f4946ae369a84e6fc40184595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />, but the bill is halved, so you need to draw only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07acdb21ef213686516af033784fad961497677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />.) We see that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of each bill <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/6739c8a3ef02d0f557bfbe01c9c92e562ff9a7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2668276d1c41b9274742bfcc30aef16cee0265bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1af88c1534bab510152766fb60851db0c3a5af52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555360df10d7f3448442d43c277f763b0d1236bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" />.\nThus, we can easily see the solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/379e1de875729985bfe2f8707bd43996f4d1e519.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D) \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"56\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Quick_and_simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Quick_and_simple)\">Solution 6 (Quick and simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Quick and simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that either we draw two different types of bills or two of the same. If we draw two different types of bills, \nthere are simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/54216aeffa0fa278199cd3ceeb64cc8400c4a8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"39\" height=\"55\" /> ways and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways if we have two of the same. \nCounting up the possibilities where it is more than 20, namely being:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80c86210901864dfccfb8f8680d77433b5a83ea5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1, 20\\]\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/0311346226c65545653ff50a81d79477526c565f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5, 20\\]\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717a6581c0e84a3a1bc953926f8ee1884910e172.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10, 10\\]\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f11e2d5d305d1d70b7a2a9193d420469a43fa1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10, 20\\]\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />\nand finally, 20, 20. Now, we see that we have five possibilities out of 10, which gives us the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/379e1de875729985bfe2f8707bd43996f4d1e519.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D) \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"56\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7EOwpzC9C74\">https://youtu.be/7EOwpzC9C74</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></spa